 **Data Structures:**
 The core structure `SectionStorage` contains a single field `data` of type `Representation`, an enum with three variants:
-
-1.  `Representation::Empty`: Holds no data. Used when all 4096 voxels are air (ID 0) [S1, unofficial].
-2.  `Representation::Uniform`: Holds a single `VoxelId`. Used when all 4096 voxels share the same non-zero ID [S1, unofficial].
-3.  `Representation::Palette`: Holds a `Palette` struct:
-    -   `entries`: A `Vec<PaletteEntry>`. Each `PaletteEntry` is a struct with two fields: `id` (4 bytes, `VoxelId`) and `count` (2 bytes, `u16`) [S1, unofficial]. Total size per entry is 6 bytes, packed sequentially [S1, unofficial].
-    -   `words`: A `Vec<u64>` containing the bit-packed palette indices.
-    -   `bits`: A `u8` indicating the number of bits used to store each index (1–12) [S1, unofficial].
